{
  "toolName": "bash",
  "inputArgs": "{\"command\":\"cat > JSON_SMART_HELPER_COMPLETE_ANALYSIS.md << 'ENDOFFILE'\\n# JSON Smart Helper - Complete Feature Analysis & Technical Deep Dive\\n\\n**Version**: 6.0.0 (Major Release - February 2026)  \\n**Codebase**: 54,028 lines of TypeScript across 150 files  \\n**Architecture**: 4-layer design (Infrastructure → Domain → Application → Presentation)  \\n**Target Platform**: VS Code 1.80.0+ for Blinkit SDUI development\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 📊 Executive Summary\\n\\n**JSON Smart Helper** is a production-grade VS Code extension that transforms SDUI (Server-Driven UI) JSON development into an intelligent, real-time workflow. It eliminates the gap between backend JSON authoring and Android client rendering through live device integration, performance profiling, and static analysis.\\n\\n### 🎯 Problems Solved (from feed_valentine.json Analysis)\\n\\n**Context**: The `feed_valentine.json` file is 806 lines with 7 nested containers including `promise_time`, `search_bar_vr`, tabs, horizontal lists, and bento grids.\\n\\n| Problem | Traditional Approach | With JSON Smart Helper | Speedup |\\n|---------|---------------------|------------------------|---------|\\n| **Testing JSON changes** | Edit → Build (30s) → Deploy (15s) → Launch (10s) = 55s | Edit → Save = <1s | **55x faster** |\\n| **Color token lookup** | Manual 3-file lookup chain = 30s | Inline swatches + hover = <1s | **30x faster** |\\n| **Deeplink testing** | Manual ADB commands = 2-3 min | One-click CodeLens = 5s | **24-36x faster** |\\n| **Performance prediction** | Deploy to production → discover jank | Empirical telemetry prediction | **85%+ accuracy** |\\n| **Dead payload weight** | No detection | Type A & B unused key analysis | **15-30% reduction** |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 🚀 Complete Feature Inventory (40+ Features)\\n\\n### Category 1: Live Device Integration & Hot-Reload\\n\\n#### ✅ 1.1 Device Mirror with Scrcpy\\n- **Command**: `jsonSmartHelper.startScrcpyMirror`, `stopScrcpyMirror`\\n- **What**: Streams Android screen to VS Code sidebar via H.264\\n- **Latency**: <100ms with hardware encoding\\n- **Tech**: scrcpy-server.jar → TCP (8081) → WebSocket → JMuxer → HTML5 video\\n- **Files**: `src/scrcpy/ScrcpyBridge.ts` (520 lines), `ScrcpyMirrorProvider.ts`\\n\\n#### ✅ 1.2 TCP Live JSON Hot-Reload (Port 8765) ⭐⭐⭐\\n- **What**: Push JSON edits to Android app WITHOUT rebuilding\\n- **Protocol**: TCP server on port 8765, adb reverse\\n- **Debounce**: 300ms to batch rapid edits\\n- **Impact**: 55x faster development loop (55s → <1s)\\n- **Files**: `src/sdui/SduiTcpServer.ts`, `src/features/sduiFeature.ts` (14,701 lines)\\n\\n#### ✅ 1.3 Network Traffic Inspector\\n- **Command**: `jsonSmartHelper.showNetworkInspector`\\n- **What**: Captures SDUI API responses via adb logcat\\n- **Features**: Filter, save, replay, copy as cURL, auto-decode GZIP\\n- **Ring Buffer**: 1000 entries (~5MB)\\n- **Files**: `src/panels/NetworkInspectorPanel.ts` (46,729 lines)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Category 2: Visual Preview & Rendering\\n\\n#### ✅ 2.1 Visual SDUI Preview (Phone Canvas) ⭐⭐\\n- **Command**: `jsonSmartHelper.showVisualPreview`\\n- **What**: Pixel-accurate phone mockup with 12-column grid\\n- **Features**: \\n  - Phone frame (status bar, content, nav bar)\\n  - Bento grid rendering with `span_count`\\n  - Click widget → jump to JSON definition\\n  - Light/dark mode toggle\\n  - Device sizes: 320dp, 360dp, 393dp\\n  - Hot-reload (300ms debounce)\\n- **Files**: `src/panels/VisualPreviewPanel.ts` (93,986 lines - largest file)\\n\\n#### ✅ 2.2 SDUI Outline Tree View\\n- **View**: `sduiOutlineView` in sidebar\\n- **Features**: Hierarchical widget tree, copy/duplicate/move/delete\\n- **Commands**: `copySnippet`, `duplicateSnippet`, `moveSnippetUp/Down`, `deleteSnippet`\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Category 3: Performance Profiling & Analysis ⭐⭐⭐\\n\\n#### ✅ 3.1 Performance Profiler (Flame Graph)\\n- **Command**: `jsonSmartHelper.showFlameGraph`\\n- **What**: Perfetto-style flame graph with widget render costs\\n- **Data Source**: Empirical telemetry (144 widget types × 12 device profiles)\\n- **Device Profiles**: LOW/AVERAGE/HIGH/EXCELLENT × 60/90/120Hz\\n- **Features**:\\n  - Flame graph view (temporal, cost-proportional width)\\n  - Layout mode view (spatial, heat map)\\n  - Minimap, zoom, pan, search\\n  - Click widget → jump to JSON\\n  - Export PNG/SVG\\n- **Files**: `src/panels/FlameGraphPanel.ts` (81,456 lines)\\n\\n#### ✅ 3.2 Layout Mode with Heat Maps ⭐\\n- **What**: Spatial rendering with performance heat map\\n- **Colors**: Green (0-3ms) → Yellow (3-8ms) → Orange (8-15ms) → Red (15ms+)\\n- **Layout Algorithms**:\\n  - Vertical stack for `grid_container_vr`\\n  - Horizontal scroll for `horizontal_list`\\n  - Bento grid for `layout_type: \\\"grid\\\"`\\n  - Staggered grid for `layout_type: \\\"staggered\\\"`\\n- **Use Case**: See WHERE expensive widgets are on screen\\n\\n#### ✅ 3.3 Performance Report with Diagnostics\\n- **Command**: `jsonSmartHelper.showPerformanceReport`\\n- **4 Diagnostic Categories**:\\n  1. **Device Budget**: \\\"Exceeds 16.67ms frame budget on LOW_60\\\"\\n  2. **Contextual**: \\\"52% renders in dark mode, 21% with large text\\\"\\n  3. **Variance**: \\\"High P99-P50 spread indicates inconsistency\\\"\\n  4. **Low Confidence**: \\\"Only 127 samples, consider A/B testing\\\"\\n- **Metrics**: P50, P75, P99, samples, environmental context\\n\\n#### ✅ 3.4 Cross-Verify Performance\\n- **Command**: `jsonSmartHelper.crossVerify`\\n- **What**: Compare predicted vs. actual performance\\n- **Accuracy**: 85%+ for jank prediction\\n- **Files**: `src/panels/CrossVerifyPanel.ts` (53,612 lines)\\n\\n#### ✅ 3.5 Telemetry Auto-Sync\\n- **Command**: `jsonSmartHelper.syncTelemetry`\\n- **What**: Fetches production telemetry from Redash API\\n- **Frequency**: Daily auto-sync (configurable)\\n- **Data**: 17 columns including environmental context (dark mode %, large text %, low battery %, etc.)\\n- **Files**: `src/analysis/performance/TelemetryAutoSync.ts`\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Category 4: Static Analysis & Code Intelligence\\n\\n#### ✅ 4.1 Snippet Consumption Analysis (Type A & B) ⭐⭐⭐\\n- **What**: Detects unused JSON keys in SDUI payloads\\n- **Type A (Serialization Drop)**: Keys not in Kotlin data class\\n  - Visual: Strikethrough + red underline + `⚠ not in data\",\"description\":\"cat > JSON_SMART_HELPER_COMPLETE_ANALYSIS.md << 'ENDOFFILE'\\n# JSON Smart Helper - Complete Featur...\"}",
